 StyleBox["complex", "TI"],
 " is perfect on chain level."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"2fdca935-b535-4efb-803d-5b771a2955b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pairing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["w", "TI"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"v", "w"}], "TI"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fb4dfc42-4604-4185-adbc-7598a84b1f26"],
 " of a model of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c1db04e0-62ea-4223-9b34-8ff981af511d"],
 " is perfect on chain level when the model vanishes above degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "318d0c68-3032-4263-a05d-a93a7e83dcfe"],
 " and pairs degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "937792c2-fa57-4b0a-8726-2caa11607fa6"],
 " nondegenerately with degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca179ee2-74af-45ba-b648-da1132100671"],
 " for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "902b35c2-dbf0-441c-863d-19415d8238e5"],
 ". The model is then a dPD algebra."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the predicate is the chain-level counterpart \
of PoincareDualityQ and, unlike it, exact on a model: a model is \
finite-dimensional exactly when every generator of even degree is truncated, \
so the answer is False when one is not, and otherwise every degree up to the \
finite top is checked (H1, 2026-09-24). A True makes a model a dPD algebra \
and a complex a cyclic cochain complex, and the name says the property rather \
than either structure; no alternative name was recorded. Prior art: the \
Wolfram Language has no pairing on a graded algebra; the test is the \
MatrixRank of the Gram matrix between degree k and degree n-k. The engine the \
verification suites load has no such test; the suites pin this predicate over \
the catalogue, where exactly the exterior algebras have a perfect pairing on \
chain level, and on T^2 oriented in degree 1.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
 CellID->533075080,ExpressionUUID->"7c34017d-1095-4cfc-8435-de4cbf078ad1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A model with a generator of even degree that no truncation bounds is \
infinite-dimensional, and the answer is ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d533c5c4-af05-4297-bff3-a77f7f9f307d"],
 ". Otherwise the model is finite-dimensional, every degree is checked, and \
the test is exact."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"42290cf1-b330-4e09-b3ae-d46fd04ca464"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A complex of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a0b093c-4a2a-4b2b-ba34-54ca6d484f00"],
 " has a perfect pairing when it pairs degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8e198c6a-4a0f-48a2-a89d-851d5dda8182"],
 " nondegenerately with degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "baf4b3ea-bee2-4ec6-a7f6-71ca30e9ecd5"],
 " for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a0d3a203-f769-4162-bbc0-d6123c412365"],
 ". It is then a cyclic cochain complex, and a dPD algebra when it carries a \
product."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"35b3531e-1162-4bdc-b620-cc107e7b6562"],

Cell["\<\
A perfect pairing on chain level has no degenerate subspace, so the model or \
complex is its own nondegenerate quotient.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"aac63934-3532-4a42-bad6-f712a6a0d602"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A perfect pairing on chain level induces one on cohomology, so a ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0dd7f8d-cdda-4031-ab90-b8369e872b57"],
 " here implies a ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d7879be-ab40-4892-b211-83578bc5fb29"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["PoincareDualityQ"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/PoincareDualityQ",
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6d8a3021-ee7a-4e50-858f-1ed7d24464ce"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e37a1605-7196-439b-8612-ec97f4e39bae"]
}, Open  ]],

